PASSPORTS -
Applications are accepted Monday-Friday, 9:00 am - 3:00 pm, by appointment only. Please call the Town Clerk's office (401-647-2822 x. 100) to schedule an appointment. The Town Clerk’s Office is a passport acceptance facility. Normal processing of a passport can take up to 6 weeks. Processing can be expedited to 2-3 weeks for an additional fee of $60.00. Authorization of both parents is required for children under 18 years old. Applicants must appear in person, including children.
Passport Fees:Age 16 and Over – Total fee is $165.00 ($130.00 application fee payable to US Department of State and $35.00 processing fee payable to the Town of Scituate)
Under age 16 – Total fee is $135.00 ($100.00 application fee payable to US Department of State and $35.00 processing fee payable to the Town of Scituate)The application fee must be paid by check or money order. The processing fee can be paid by cash or check.Visit www.travel.state.gov for required documents and applications.
DOG LICENSESDogs are required to be registered every April. A valid rabies certificate is required at the time of registration. Scituate residents are entitled to register no more than 3 dogs per residence. The fee is $10.00 per dog. Licenses may be obtained at the Town Clerk’s office during normal business hours. Traditionally, each April the Town holds a rabies clinic where dogs & cats can receive their rabies shot at reduced rates. Licenses for dogs may also be obtained at the clinic. Dates, times, and other details will be posted on the Online Town Calendar.
YARD SALESPursuant to the Scituate Code of Ordinance a yard sale may be held for the sale of typically second-hand personal, household and/or garden property. Any town resident desiring to hold such a sale on their property must apply to the Town Clerk for a yard sale license. The license fee is $5.00. Each resident is allowed to hold 2 yard sales a year on their property.
TRADE NAME
A recent change to the state’s Trade Name law now requires all Trade Names registered before December 31, 2025 to file a free renewal with the RI Department of State to keep the Trade Name active. The filing period runs from September 1 to November 30, 2026, and the required filing can be submitted online.
A Trade Name is a business name used by sole proprietorships and general partnerships to conduct business in a particular RI city or town. The renewal filing requirement is in conjunction with the transfer of all Trade Names from City and Town Clerk’s offices to the RI Department of State’s Business Services Division. All new Trade Names will be registered with the Business Services Division.
Visit https://www.sos.ri.gov/divisions/business-services/ri-trade-names to submit a renewal filing for an eligible Trade Name or contact the Business Services Division at 401-222-3040 or corporations@sos.ri.gov for assistance.

